  "cells": [
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "# 00 — Setup: Variables, Secret & Heat Limit\n\nBefore deploying the weather station labs, configure your broker with:\n1. **Four environment variables** and **one secret** (so coordinates and mail settings aren't hardcoded in your LoT code).\n2. **The initial heat alert threshold** (`30` °C) as a retained MQTT message on `config/heat_limit_c`.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Set environment variables & secret\n\n1. Click **`root`** in the **top-right corner** of the HUB and select **Command Console**.\n2. Copy and run these five commands **one line at a time** (press **Enter** after each line):\n\n```text\n-setEnv WEATHER_LAT=40.7128\n-setEnv WEATHER_LON=-74.0060\n-setEnv SMTP_HOST=mailpit\n-setEnv SMTP_USER=weather@example.com\n-setSecret SMTP_PASSWORD=any-password\n```\n\n- Keep the `NAME=value` format with **no spaces** around `=`.\n- Your LoT code will read these values using `GET ENV \"...\"` and `GET SECRET \"...\"`.\n- **Verify:** Open **`root` (top right) → Broker Settings → Variables & Secrets** to see your 4 variables and 1 secret (`SMTP_PASSWORD` is write-only, so its value stays hidden).\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Publish the initial heat limit (`30` °C)\n\nIn Lab 4, the `HeatAlert` Action reads the temperature threshold from `config/heat_limit_c`. Publishing it with **Retain ON** stores the value on the broker so any Action can read it immediately with `GET TOPIC \"config/heat_limit_c\"`.\n\n1. Open **Data Viewer** from the **bottom Dock**.\n2. Click the **Publish** button (paper-plane icon) to open the publish drawer.\n3. Fill in:\n   - **Topic:** `config/heat_limit_c`\n   - **Payload:** `30`\n   - **Retain:** **ON** (important — without Retain, the broker won't remember the value between messages)\n4. Click **Publish**.\n\n---\n\n**Next up:** Open **`01-heartbeat.lotnb`** in the left sidebar to deploy your first LoT Action!"
    }
  ]
}
